<XuiHtmlElement>
<Properties>
<Id>XuiHtmlElement1</Id>
<Width>544.000000</Width>
<Height>312.000000</Height>
<Position>24.000000,56.000000,0.000000</Position>
<Text>&lt;font color="#000000" size=11&gt;

All of the text descriptions in this demo are created using the &lt;i&gt;&lt;b&gt;HTML Element&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/i&gt;.
The HTML support in XUI is a lite and strict version of what is used in web pages.
It supports the core tags for text formatting, images, list variations, and tables.

</Text>
</Properties>
</XuiHtmlElement>
<XuiBackButton>
<Properties>
<Id>XuiBackButton1</Id>
<Width>184.000000</Width>
<Height>40.000000</Height>
<Position>16.000000,376.000000,0.000000</Position>
<DisableFocusRecursion>true</DisableFocusRecursion>
<UnfocusedInput>true</UnfocusedInput>
<Text>Back Button</Text>
<PressKey>22593</PressKey>
</Properties>
</XuiBackButton>
<XuiHtmlControl>
<Properties>
<Id>XuiHtmlControl1</Id>
<Width>512.000000</Width>
<Height>208.000000</Height>
<Position>48.000000,152.000000,0.000000</Position>
<Visual>XuiHtmlControl_ScrollV</Visual>
<NavDown>navNext1</NavDown>
<Text>&lt;font size=12&gt;

&lt;a name="top"&gt;This&lt;/a&gt; &lt;i&gt;&lt;b&gt;HTML Control&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/i&gt; can also handle user input, which adds the capability for anchor tags (ie. links).
&lt;ol type=I&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="goto_bookmarks"&gt;Bookmarks&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="goto_visited"&gt;Visited Links&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="goto_placeholders"&gt;Placeholder Images&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="goto_tags"&gt;Supported Tags&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;

&lt;br/&gt;

&lt;table bgcolor="#cccccc"&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td width="10"/&gt;
&lt;td&gt;
&lt;b&gt;Bookmarks:&lt;/b&gt;
&lt;a href="top"&gt;(back to top)&lt;/a&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;br/&gt;

&lt;a name="goto_bookmarks"&gt;Anchors&lt;/a&gt; have built-in bookmarking support to jump from one section of HTML to another, but the application needs to handle other behaviors such as navigating to a new scene.

&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;br/&gt;

&lt;table bgcolor="#cccccc"&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td width="10"/&gt;
&lt;td&gt;
&lt;b&gt;Visited Links:&lt;/b&gt;
&lt;a href="top"&gt;(back to top)&lt;/a&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;br/&gt;

&lt;a name="goto_visited"&gt;An&lt;/a&gt; application can also handle a message in order to change links to a visited color (similar to a web browser).
The application needs to maintain the links that have been visited, and pass back the appropriate value when requested.

&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;br/&gt;

&lt;table bgcolor="#cccccc"&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td width="10"/&gt;
&lt;td&gt;
&lt;b&gt;Placeholder Images:&lt;/b&gt;
&lt;a href="top"&gt;(back to top)&lt;/a&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;br/&gt;

&lt;a name="goto_placeholders"&gt;A&lt;/a&gt; message is also sent to the parent application whenever an image is requested from the HTML.
This allows the application to tell the HTML to use a different image instead, if the requested one is not yet available... and it also enables multiple replacement images, if desired.

&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;br/&gt;

&lt;table bgcolor="#cccccc"&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td width="10"/&gt;
&lt;td&gt;
&lt;b&gt;Supported Tags:&lt;/b&gt;
&lt;a href="top"&gt;(back to top)&lt;/a&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;br/&gt;

&lt;a name="goto_tags"&gt;Please &lt;/a&gt; see the XUI documentation for the full set of tags supported by this lite version of HTML.

&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;br/&gt;

&lt;/font&gt;

</Text>
</Properties>
</XuiHtmlControl>
</XuiScene>
</XuiCanvas>
